    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1269">

                <pb facs="1254" n="1244" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1244"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/4–2249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-22T19:00:00+08:00">April 22, 1949—7
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 22—5:45 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1310. Garrison Commander today informed meeting of foreign representatives
                    attended by AMA and ANA<anchor n="63" xml:id="d1269-f1"/> [that] women and
                    children should be removed to safer areas since state of war now exists <pb
                        facs="1255" n="1245" xml:id="pg1245"/> in Shanghai area. He stated in his
                    opinion major assault on Shanghai was not imminent presumably because Communists
                    must regroup after river crossing. He emphasized however Shanghai would be
                    defended come what might and that due to Communist infiltrations riots might
                    break out at any moment.</p>
                <p>Remytel 1309, April 22, 6 p. m., repeated Nanking 756, would appreciate immediate
                    authority to publicize General Chen’s statement and to emphasize that American
                    community should be guided accordingly.<anchor n="64" xml:id="d1269-f2"/> If
                    granted I shall try to act in concert with Consular colleagues.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Nanking 757.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1269-f1" n="63" xml:id="d1269-f1-content">
                <p>Assistant Military and Naval Attachés, respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1269-f2" n="64" xml:id="d1269-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 717, April 22, 4 p. m., the Department replied: “Authority
                    requested urtel 1310, April 22 granted.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
